        <h2 id="verdict">The verdict</h2>
        <p>
          IPTV in the UK is a straightforward trade. You give up the dish and the engineer visit, and you
          get one bill instead of four with nothing renewing behind your back. It works if your line
          clears 15 Mbps at peak and you are willing to spend fifteen minutes with a Fire Stick and a
          player app. It does not work if your broadband is the problem, and any provider telling you
          otherwise is not worth £{site.price}.
        </p>
        <p>
          Start on the month. Run the weekend test. If it holds up, the annual plan is £49.99 and works
          out at £4.17 a month, and if it does not, you have seven days to say so.
          <a href={waLink('Hi, I read the IPTV UK guide. I would like to start on the one-month plan.')} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">Message us on WhatsApp</a>
          and we answer in under two minutes during UK hours, which I mention because that is the bit you
          will actually use.
        </p>
        <p>
          And if it is still stuttering after the cable, the 5 GHz switch and the router reboot, it is not
          the box. It is the router your ISP posted you in 2016, sat behind a mirror in the hallway, doing
          its best.
        </p>
